jection); both sides underscored their projections, so the game ran colder than either team's numbers said."},{"title":"Where the result sat in the simulations","body":"Total: 26 against 53.4 projected (-27.4), about the 4th percentile of the simulated totals (a typical game swings ±15.5).\n\nMargin: Seminoles by 6 against Panthers by 0.7 projected, about the 33rd percentile of the simulated margins (typical swing ±15.3).\n\nAn unusual result, but one the simulations saw regularly (roughly one game in six to one in twenty)."},{"title":"Situational factors, checked","body":"Weather (40°F · ? mph wind): Panthers ×0.94, Seminoles ×0.94."},{"title":"Against the market","body":"PITT ML (-148) at -148: the algo gave it 57% vs 57% fair (-0.6 pts) — lost (-1u); lost to the close (closing fair chance 58%). FSU ML (+124) at +124: the algo gave it 43% vs 43% fair (+0.6 pts) — won (+1.2u); lost to the close (closing fair chance 42%). PITT -3 (-108) at -108: the algo gave it 49% vs 50% fair (-0.6 pts) — lost (-1u); same number as the close. FSU +3 (-112) at -112: the algo gave it 51% vs 50% fair (+0.6 pts) — won (+0.9u); same number as the close. OVER 52.5 (-108) at -108: the algo gave it 49% vs 50% fair (-0.1 pts) — lost (-1u); same number as the close. UNDER 52.5 (-112) at -112: the algo gave it 51% vs 50% fair (+0.1 pts) — won (+0.9u); same number as the close.\n\nThe line barely moved between the algo's snapshot and the close.\n\nNo bet: nothing cleared the algo's bar before the game."},{"title":"Where the public and the money were","body":"Splits (Action Network): spread: 53% of bets on Seminoles, 78% of the money — Seminoles covered; total: 58% of bets on the over, 62% of the money — it went under; moneyline: 19% of bets on Seminoles, 37% of the money.\n\nThe sharp side by the algo's read was Seminoles, who won and covered."},{"title":"What the algo learns","body":"This game's own lesson: scoring came in at ×0.476 of the raw projection, and the home side beat its projected